meta {
  name: PhoneOS Cloud API: Dial
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: https://webexapis.com/v1/xapi/command/Call.Dial
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  Content-Type: application/json
  Authorization: Bearer {{workspacetoken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "deviceId": "{{webexDeviceId}}",
    "arguments": {
      "Line": 1,
      "Number": "+18005532447"
    }
  }
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: false
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  Sends a "Call.Dial" xAPI command directly to a specific Workspace/Room device — the PhoneOS/RoomOS
  xAPI command-execution endpoint. Unlike the personal-line Dial request, this bypasses user
  profiles entirely and targets hardware directly.

  **Parameters/Headers**
  - `Authorization` — bound to `{{workspacetoken}}` (placeholder). Can be a user token via an
    integration, or a Service App token — either way it needs the `spark:xapi_commands` scope. This
    credential cannot control personal devices.

  **Body** (`body:json`)
  - `deviceId` — bound to `{{webexDeviceId}}`; the target device's ID (from "List Devices" in this
    folder — note this is the plain device `id`/`webexDeviceId`, not `callingDeviceId`).
  - `arguments.Line` — the line/appearance on the device to use.
  - `arguments.Number` — the number to dial.

  Used for Workspace Devices (Room Kits, Boards, MPP phones) — ideal for in-room automation, digital
  signage, and remote hardware management.

  Reference: https://developer.webex.com/docs/api/v1/xapi/execute-command

  Per-command xAPI reference: https://roomos.cisco.com/xapi/Command.Dial/
  (also: https://phoneos.cisco.com/xapi?release=ebce6e9968ba7924022bef9285c67cae50af6915&domain=Call&object=Call+Dial)

  ---
  *Documentation written by AI (Claude) as a companion to the WebexOne 2026 API Overview session.*
}
